# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# What this file is actually deciding
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This repository is THE COURSE, not one person's copy of it. So everything the
# course ships is tracked — including every reference solution and every quiz
# answer key, which is where a lot of the teaching lives:
#
#     challenge/solution/*.php    the reference implementation
#     challenge/checks.php        the assertions that do the grading
#     quiz/QUIZ.md                answer key in the <details> block at the foot
#
# None of that is ignored and none of it should be.
#
# What IS ignored is one particular learner's work. `check.php` grades by
# running the learner's domain/workshop/ against the course's checks.php, so
# grading works perfectly for somebody who has cloned this and written nothing.
# But if a completed domain/workshop/ were committed, a fresh clone would report
# Module 1 as finished before its owner had opened a file.
#
# If you want your own work under version control, keep it on a separate branch
# that removes these two rules, or run `git init` inside domain/workshop/.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The learner's answers to the code challenges. See above.
/domain/workshop/*.php
/domain/workshop/**/*.php

# Same, for the infrastructure layer, from Lesson 3.1 onwards.
/infrastructure/*.php
/infrastructure/**/*.php

# The learner's progress record. PROGRESS.template.md is tracked; copy it.
/PROGRESS.md

# The learner's answers to the written challenges — Module 0, and the follow-up
# questions at the foot of every challenge. Deliberately without a key: a
# published set of model answers would spoil an exercise whose whole value is
# forming the argument yourself.
my-answers.md
my-glossary.md
/notes/

# Composer — needed from Module 3, never committed
/vendor/

# PHPUnit
/.phpunit.cache/

# Scratch output from the harness
/solution-output/

# SQLite databases created by Module 3's integration tests
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
